   "AC2 contradicted: the documented command `clojure -M:run -- --help` exits 1 with 'Unknown command: --help'",
   :file "src/epiphany/infra/main.clj",
   :detail
   "AC: 'clojure -M:run -- --help succeeds and identifies the canonical executable as epiphany; ep invokes the same entry point.' Measured: `clojure -M:run -- --help` → stdout 'Unknown command: --help' + usage, exit 1. Root cause verified empirically: the Clojure CLI passes the literal `--` through to `-main` (confirmed with a scratch -m project: args arrive as (\"--\" \"--help\")), and tools.cli (`cli/parse-opts args global-options :in-order true`, main.clj:1252) treats `--` as end-of-options, so `--help` lands in `arguments` and falls into the unknown-command branch (main.clj:1287-1288). Nothing in main.clj's history ever stripped a leading `--`. The same documented `--` separator breaks worse elsewhere: `clojure -M:run -- ingest <path> --profile services` dies in clojure.main with FileNotFoundException \"--\". This exact broken command is documented in AGENTS.md:17 and README.md:190, so every agent/user following the repo's own instructions hits it. Mitigating evidence: help itself works — `bin/ep --help` and `clojure -M:run --help` exit 0 and identify both `epiphany` and the `ep` alias, and bin/ep + bin/epiphany exec the same entry point — but the criterion's literal command does not succeed.",
